<Base title="Zero Bite Privacy Policy" description="Zero Bite privacy policy: your food list stays on your device. No account, no ads, no tracking." section="zerobite">
  <p class="overline">Privacy policy · Effective 7 October 2026</p>
  <h1>Your food stays on your phone</h1>
  <p class="lead">Zero Bite has no account, no advertising, no analytics and no tracking. We don't collect, sell or share your personal data.</p>

  <h2>What's stored on your iPhone</h2>
  <p>The food you add (names, brands, barcodes, quantities, dates, storage place and notes), your settings (reminder times, allergies, recall checks) and a copy of recent food recall alerts. This is stored only on your device and included in your normal iPhone or iCloud backups. We can't see it.</p>

  <h2>Camera and photos</h2>
  <p>When you scan a label or choose a photo, the text and barcode are read on your iPhone using Apple's Vision framework. Images are not saved and never leave your device.</p>

  <h2>What leaves your iPhone</h2>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>Barcode lookups (Open Food Facts)</strong>
  <p>When you scan a barcode, only the barcode number is sent to <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/">Open Food Facts</a>, a free public food database, to find the product's name and brand. No other information about you or your fridge is sent. Open Food Facts handles requests under its own <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>Food recall alerts (Food Standards Agency)</strong>
  <p>If recall checks are on, Zero Bite downloads the UK Food Standards Agency's public list of recent alerts. Nothing about you, your food or your allergies is sent; matching happens on your iPhone. You can turn this off in Settings → Food safety.</p>
  </div>
  <p>Like any internet request, these services can see your device's IP address. We don't run any servers and receive none of this information.</p>

  <h2>Notifications</h2>
  <p>Expiry reminders and recall warnings are local notifications created on your iPhone. They aren't sent through our servers or any push service.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Zero Bite doesn't collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>Go to Settings → Data → Delete everything in the app, or delete the app to remove all of its data from your iPhone.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the effective date above. If Zero Bite ever starts collecting data, we'll ask for your permission first.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:support@mazesys.com?subject=Zero%20Bite%20privacy">support@mazesys.com</a>.</p>
</Base>
